A||||10||ThatRickGuy||It Runs!!! :) :) :) :) :)||||10||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||09:57 PM||||Heya everyone! I got it running! The 3.2 that is. woowho! I need to get the timing set perfect, the shop didn't have a working timing light  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and I need to put my new exhaust bolts on which are ariving tomorrow from the fiero store (next day deliery rocks!) Only have 2 problems. An intermitant code 44 (it came on during the 20 minute break in, then went away after I let the car sit for a few seconds looking for a code book, and then it popped up again later right when I was pulling out of the shop, but it disappeared again after a few seconds) And my temp guage is sitting at pegged 0  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I put a new sensor in. The wire clip looks burnt and chipped, but there's no sign of a short or anything. oh wait, there is one more thing... the damn Dinger won't stop beeping!!!! I remeber seeing a post on that a few months ago, so I'm off to drege threw the archives. Thanks for all the help and advise. and once I get this engine broke in, I'll get the performance numbers back to you all.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Bill H||10-19-2000||10:01 PM|||| What else did you do? I have been thinking of doing the 3.2 swap too. Will you be getting offical time slips? I would like to know 1/4 times with that set up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||10-19-2000||10:24 PM||||Good going!!!  I know the feeling of firing up a new engine - exciting and scary - hoping you didn't screw something up.  I had a couple problems, had to change the MAP and O2 sensor to solve poor idling, but yours sounds like it went without a hitch.<P>The real fun starts once you start driving it, and everything "feels right and works right".  Happy motoring<P>3.4L  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||10:26 PM||||I'm not planing on the 1/4 at the moment. But my machnest had never built up a fiero engine befor so she's super curious and said she could hook me up with some guys w/ a dyno and all the sniffing equipment to make sure it's running perfect.<P>as for what I did, well, I'm not big on open road racing. sorry going 150 mph just isn't that much fun (risk of instant death and/or loss of license and all..) so I went for torque. I got a 3.1 crank, bored the cylinders .030 over, 3 angle vale job, and basically just a clean up/status quo rebuild from there. <P>And it looks like the forum has saved me time again. The chime is mostlikely going off from the e-brake (light is stuck on) which I never use (joys of have an auto). The code 44 is exhaust lean, but considering the gas that's in the car, the exhaust leaks, and slightly off timing, that should be cleared up after tomorrow's timing/exhaust work, and the gas should be cleaned up by next week when I get a fresh tank. I'll throw some fuel cleaner in there for now.<P>Pennock, you are the man for starting this forum! And Ogre, you're a genious! heheh the offer for a free beer is extended to both of you if ya ever get to the washinton DC area (kinda a long drive for ya cliff, and watch out for that big puddle, I think they named it the atlantic)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill H||10-19-2000||10:31 PM||||I am not looking for top end either. I would like a 1/4 mile time in the 13's though. This sounds like a lot but a stock tran am will do it. Just want to know that I would be safe from 90% of those damn import guys. You all know the ones.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||10:32 PM||||just out of curiocity... what's the v6 suposed to idle at? mine was bouncing arround a little between 800-1000, I'm guessing it's because of the timing and ECM arguing. Anyways, I can't wait to get out of the break in phase to see what she can do!||||reg||1
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||11:33 PM||||more progress has just been made  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I went back out to put the right plates on the fiero. I looked under the car to check for any fluid leaks and I saw a hose hanging down. pushed it back up, and low and behold it was the EGR vacuum line. hooked that back up. poped the clip off the ebrake and started her up. no ding and no slight miss!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> unfortunatly the fiero is idling at arround 1500 rpms now in park, I forgot to check in gear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'm fearfull that it's the EGR tube because that thing is so dang expencive. (something like $75 for the flex tube, $100 for the stock) hopefully if that is the problem I can still weld it back into funcitoning condition. ahh well, I'm still estatic to have a fiero that runs!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||10-20-2000||11:47 AM||||Sounds awesome, Now I want to go yank the engine out of mine. <P>I hate to break it to you but I haven't found a flexible EGR tube for less than $90, Rodney Dickman has them if you do end up needing one.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
